SWARM 4b — stop the dq-auditor flood against delisted tickers.
Repo: signaldeck · branch hmm-regime-and-pbo · base HEAD 0b1f73b

TARGET FILES
  daemon/internal/store/survivorship.go       (modified — adds Store.DQSilencedSymbols)
  daemon/internal/maintain/maintain.go        (modified — DQAuditor.Run skips silenced symbols)
  daemon/internal/maintain/dqdelisted_test.go (NEW — pins the skip and all three exemptions)

HOW TO APPLY (from the repo root: C:/Users/Nicholas_N/Desktop/claude code/signaldeck)
  git apply --check round2-drafts/patches/dq-auditor-delisted.patch   # verify first
  git apply         round2-drafts/patches/dq-auditor-delisted.patch
Standard -p1 paths. Reverse with `git apply -R`. Touches no locked file.

WHAT LAYER THIS IS: A SYMPTOM MASK, DELIBERATELY. NOT THE ROOT FIX.
The root fault is BLOCKED-6: 1,868 permanently-delisted rows carry active=1.
pipeline/delisting.go:152 -> store.MarkDelisted (survivorship.go:192) writes
symbols.delisted_at and never clears `active`, by explicit design ("delisting is
a MARKET fact, deactivating is a SUBSCRIPTION decision"). The consequence is that
~45 callers of ListSymbols(ctx,true) — every scorer, poller, trainer and agent in
the fleet, not only this auditor — iterate 1,868 dead tickers. THIS PATCH FIXES
ONE OF THOSE 45 CONSUMERS. It does not repair the universe and must not be
reported as having done so.

WHY IT IS STILL WORTH HAVING (defence in depth, on grounds that survive the root
fix rather than substituting for it):
  1. Freshness is UNDEFINED for a security that stopped trading. Even on a
     perfectly groomed universe, "last daily bar is 40d old" on a delisted name
     is a tautology, not an incident.
  2. DelistingDetector.Interval() is 24h, so a name is legitimately
     delisted-and-still-active for up to a day however BLOCKED-6 is resolved.
  3. The root-layer alternative — filtering delisted inside
     ListSymbols(activeOnly=true) — silently changes 45 workers at once,
     including LOCKED pipeline/paper.go, which re-admits held-but-inactive
     symbols by hand (paper.go:95-134) and would be broken by a store-level
     filter it cannot see. A 6-line guard in the one flooding worker is the
     smaller and safer change; the universe repair belongs in its own patch.

THE SKIP IS NARROW ON PURPOSE (task item 4). A delisted symbol is NOT silenced
when any of these holds:
  - the paper book holds an open position on it (a stranded position must keep
    its feed alarm — it cannot be exited without a price), or
  - it carries an unresolved score_outcomes row, or
  - it carries an unresolved prediction_outcomes row — the table
    tools/accuracy_registry.py grades for the PUBLISHED accuracy number.
The last two are separate clauses on purpose: they name the same 16 symbols
today but are written by different paths (InsertScore vs UpsertPrediction), and
a guard on a published number must not depend on that coincidence.

EVIDENCE — all read-only against data/signaldeck.db (mode=ro), 2026-08-06
  Universe:      2,950 symbols, ALL active=1; 1,868 of them delisted.
  dq_events 24h: stale=5,719 — delisted 5,599 (97.9%), live 120. 1,902 distinct
                 symbols flagged, 1,868 of them delisted.
  Hourly:        the flood STARTED at 2026-08-06 20:00Z (1,899/hr, 1,868
                 delisted). Every prior hour for 3 days ran 1-5 events/hr with
                 ZERO delisted. PREMISE CORRECTION: the reported "roughly 1,897
                 events/hour" is confirmed for the last 3 hours ONLY — it is a
                 3-hour-old regression, not a standing state.
  Overlap:       0 delisted symbols held in the paper book, 0 in `positions`,
                 0 scored in the last 30d, 16 with unresolved score_outcomes,
                 16 with unresolved prediction_outcomes (the same 16).
  Projection:    the exact query in this patch silences 1,852 of 1,868 delisted
                 rows; the audited universe goes 2,950 -> 1,098. Replayed over
                 the last 3h that removes 5,551 of 5,692 stale events (97.5%)
                 and keeps 141 (93 live + 48 delisted-but-graded).

VERIFICATION PERFORMED ON SCRATCH COPIES (never under daemon/ or research/)
